# Engineering guardrails
- Before editing, inspect the relevant files, package.json, tsconfig.json and existing project conventions. Never assume a package or API is installed.
- Preserve the current Expo SDK, React Native, routing, styling engine and gluestack-ui versions unless migration is explicitly requested.
- Make the smallest correct change; avoid unsolicited rewrites, new dependencies, extra abstraction and speculative features.
- Favor readable, testable, typed solutions over clever one-liners and artificial complexity (KISS, YAGNI).
- Prefer composition and explicit dependencies; use SOLID and DRY pragmatically, not as excuses to introduce needless layers.
- No secrets, tokens or private configuration in source code or logs. Avoid unsafe destructive commands.
- When finishing, summarize changed files, any architectural trade-offs and the validation actually performed. Never claim tests passed unless run.
